From e0560e683fde64ac6b0ff4c91893cbd43b7718e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:57:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build(xtask): cargo xtask release ports the release cut
 cross-platform

scripts/release.ps1's ten phases move into xtask (release.rs, release_bump.rs,
release_pack.rs): preflight with the same refusals (--no-tag never on main, no
tagging run, RELEASE_NOTES.md section check), the release gate tier run in
process, the workspace version bump in Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock (+ cargo
update -w and the version-lines-only guard), the two release commits, a build
of the product packages only, the post version check, sign.ps1 and the zip
staged like release.yml (NOTICE included) on Windows, installer.ps1 on
--installer. Linux, macOS and FreeBSD hand packaging to package-*.sh and
refuse --installer by name.

The cut never rebuilds xtask while it runs: the gate is called in process
(no nested cargo xtask) and the build names -p camcraft-ui/-app/-post.

release.ps1 is a thin wrapper forwarding its switches; AGENTS.md release
step 2 and the hand-test line name cargo xtask release. PROCESS_VERSION 8.

Fixes #749
Fixes #748

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
